# 4. Learning Rate ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

The learning rate controls the size of each step.

\[
\alpha
\]

---

## Learning Rate Too Small 🐌

```text
Loss
  |
  |\
  | \
  |  \
  |   \
  |____\________ Time
```

The model learns very slowly.

---

## Learning Rate Too Large 💥

The algorithm may jump over the minimum:

```text
     \       /
      \     /
       \___/
    ↗       ↘
```

It may:

- Oscillate
- Fail to converge
- Diverge

---

## Good Learning Rate

```text
Large enough → Efficient learning
Small enough → Stable convergence
```

### 🧠 Memory Trick

> **Learning rate = step size.**

