# 9. Local Minima and Saddle Points

## Local Minimum

A point that is lower than nearby points but not necessarily the lowest point globally.

## Global Minimum

The lowest possible value of the loss function.

---

## Saddle Point

A point that may look flat but is not actually a minimum.

In one direction:

```text
Down
```

In another:

```text
Up
```

High-dimensional neural-network optimization often encounters many such complex regions.

